 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 542774,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Suppose we have data that are normally distributed with mean 75 and standard deviation 5. Compute standardized scores for each of these data values: 66, 83, and 72.\n",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<br>\n<span data-math=\"−1.8\">−1.8</span><br>\n<span data-math=\"1.6\">1.6</span><br>\n<span data-math=\"−0.6\">−0.6</span>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>If <i>x</i> is a member of a normally distributed dataset with mean µ and standard deviation σ, then the standardized score for <i>x</i> is <span data-math=\"z = \\frac{{x - \\mu }}{\\sigma }\"></span>.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"z = \\frac{{x - \\mu }}{\\sigma } = \\frac{{66 - 75}}{5} = - 1.8\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"z = \\frac{{x - \\mu }}{\\sigma } = \\frac{{83 - 75}}{5} = 1.6\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"z = \\frac{{x - \\mu }}{\\sigma } = \\frac{{72 - 75}}{5} = - 0.6\"></span></p>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
